 # Changelog
 
+## 1.7.0 (2025-11-15)
+
+- Each ticket has a due time: created plus the response hours for its priority (4 urgent, 24 high, 72 normal, 168 low).
+  The hours are `RESPONSE_HOURS_*` environment variables. A ticket's due time is set once; changing the hours or the
+  ticket's priority does not move it. Tickets already in the data file get a due time from their created time and
+  priority on first load, and keep it.
+- Every ticket includes `due` when `DUE_TIMES=on`. Until then the API is unchanged, so operators can write due times
+  into the data file first. `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists open and in-progress tickets whose due time has passed.
+- The data file stays version 1 with `due` as an extra ticket field, so release 1.4.0 still loads it.
+
+## 1.6.0 (2025-10-13)
+
+- `POST /tickets/import` creates many tickets in one request (at most 5000), all of them or none, for the move from
+  the old tracker. Each imported ticket is recorded and its requester is notified as when one ticket is created.
+
+## 1.5.0 (2025-09-22)
+
+- `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns a ticket to an agent, or unassigns it. Only open and in-progress tickets can
+  change assignee; the agent is notified.
+- Every ticket includes `assignee` (`null` when unassigned). `GET /tickets` filters by `assignee`, including empty for
+  unassigned tickets.
+- The command-line listing shows each ticket's assignee.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
