+## Due times
+
+Each ticket stores `due` (created plus the `RESPONSE_HOURS_*` for its priority). Existing tickets get a due time the
+first time this release loads the data file, and the file is rewritten so it holds them. A ticket's due time does not
+move if the hours or the priority later change.
+
+Switch the API on only after the data file holds `due` on every ticket:
+
+1. Deploy this release with `DUE_TIMES` unset. The process writes due times into the data file at start. Confirm with
+   `tickets show ID` (the details include `due`) or by reading the file.
+2. Set `DUE_TIMES=on` and restart. Tickets then include `due`, and `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists open and
+   in-progress tickets whose due time has passed.
+
+If the new release misbehaves, go back to 1.4.0 on the same data file: the file stays version 1, and 1.4.0 ignores the
+extra `due` field, so every ticket still loads. Unsetting `DUE_TIMES` on this release restores the previous API without
+removing due times from the file.
+
